   "design": "A scripted extract pulls productivity figures at team level from the HR and operations systems, instead of copying them by hand. With consent, interviews are recorded and a scribe drafts the note that the psychologist corrects; notes and open answers, without names, are coded against the study codebook, and every passage is checked. Study design, the survey, interviews, analysis, discussions and the report stay with the psychologist.",
   "previous_blocker": "Figures were copied by hand and notes typed and coded by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Scripted extracts, consent-based scribes and codebook coding.",
   "still_hard": "Productivity that no system measures.",
   "human_edge": "Seeing how leadership shapes a team's results.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less copying and typing; interpretation stays.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "leadership",
     "task": "Improve the organisation",
     "learn": "Whether findings arrive sooner."
    }
